{"name":"Royal Mile","hex":"#a1a0b7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"royal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to a monarch or his (or her) family.","Having the air or demeanour of a monarch; illustrious; magnanimous; of more than common size or excellence."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A royal person; a member of a royal family.","A standard size of printing paper, measuring 25 by 20 inches."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/royal"},{"term":"mile","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The international mile: a unit of length precisely equal to 1.609344 kilometers established by treaty among Anglophone nations in 1959, divided into 5,280 feet or 1,760 yards.","Any of several customary units of length derived from the 1593 English statute mile of 8 furlongs, equivalent to 5,280 feet or 1,760 yards of various precise values."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mile"}],"entries":[{"title":"Royal Mile","blocks":[{"text":"The Royal Mile is a series of streets forming the main thoroughfare of the Old Town of Edinburgh, Scotland. The term originated in the early 20th century and has since entered popular usage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/High_Street%2C_Edinburgh.JPG/330px-High_Street%2C_Edinburgh.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Mile"},{"title":"Mile","blocks":[{"text":"The mile, sometimes the international mile or statute mile to distinguish it from other miles, is a British imperial unit and United States customary unit of length; both are based on the older English unit of length equal to 5,280 English feet, or 1,760 yards. The statute mile was standardised as a unit of length between the Commonwealth of Nations and the United States by an international agreement in 1959, when the yard was formally redefined with respect to SI units as 0.9144 metres, making the mile exactly 1609.344 metres. For everyday use, five miles equates roughly to eight kilometres. Mileage is the term used informally for a distance expressed in miles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Milestone%2C_Knightsbridge%2C_London_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1590514.jpg/330px-Milestone%2C_Knightsbridge%2C_London_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1590514.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mile"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/The_Royal_Mile%2C_Edinburgh_-_High_Resoultion.jpg/500px-The_Royal_Mile%2C_Edinburgh_-_High_Resoultion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/The_Royal_Mile%2C_Edinburgh_-_High_Resoultion.jpg/1280px-The_Royal_Mile%2C_Edinburgh_-_High_Resoultion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/The_Royal_Mile%2C_Edinburgh_-_High_Resoultion.jpg/500px-The_Royal_Mile%2C_Edinburgh_-_High_Resoultion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Castlehill forming part of the Royal Mile. The former Victorian church houses The Hub, an information service for the Edinburgh International Festival. On the right is The Scotch Whisky Experience and on the left the Camera Obscura tower and shops.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Royal_Mile%2C_Edinburgh_-_High_Resoultion.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/The_High_Street%2C_Edinburgh.JPG/500px-The_High_Street%2C_Edinburgh.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/The_High_Street%2C_Edinburgh.JPG/1280px-The_High_Street%2C_Edinburgh.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conten